# YouTube Downloader — environment (single .env.local drives the VPS deploy).
# Copy to .env.local and fill in:  cp .env.local.example .env.local

# ── YouTube cookies (optional but recommended) ────────────────────────────────
# Netscape-format cookies for YouTube so downloads bypass bot detection.
#
# Preferred: drop your exported Netscape cookies.txt next to app.py (in the app
# directory, e.g. /home/ubuntu/git/youtube-downloader/cookies.txt). The app reads
# ./cookies.txt from its current directory automatically, and deploy.sh leaves an
# existing cookies.txt untouched.
#
# Alternatively, point at a cookie file elsewhere, or paste the raw Netscape
# block (one line) here:
# COOKIES_FILE=/path/to/cookies.txt
# YOUTUBE_COOKIES=
#
# Full precedence (highest first):
#   existing cookies.txt in the app dir  >  COOKIES_FILE (path)  >  YOUTUBE_COOKIES (inline block)
# COOKIES_FILE=
# YOUTUBE_COOKIES_FILE=

# ── Optional outbound proxy for yt-dlp ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Datacenter IPs (a VPS) get flagged by YouTube with "Sign in to confirm you're
# not a bot". Routing through a residential/trusted proxy fixes it. Format any
# scheme yt-dlp supports, e.g. http://user:pass@host:port or socks5://host:port.
# YTDLP_PROXY=http://user:pass@residential-proxy.example.com:1080

# ── Port (optional, default 7860) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Must match the Cloudflare Tunnel rule.  Leave default unless 7860 is taken.
# PORT=7860

# ── Bind address (optional, default 0.0.0.0) ──────────────────────────────────
# deploy.sh sets HOST=127.0.0.1 so the VPS answers only the Cloudflare Tunnel.
# Leave unset for Docker/Render/Hugging Face, which need 0.0.0.0 to be reachable.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
